EGL 1.4 and OpenGL ES 2.0 for IRIX, on nothing but IRIX's own libGL.so
and GLX. Accelerated boards draw in hardware, unaccelerated ones through
SGI's software OpenGL. There is no software fallback: if the display
cannot do what the library needs, eglInitialize fails and says why
(egl-gles-info prints what it found).

IRIX's OpenGL is 1.1 with SGI extensions, so GLES shaders are not
compiled: each linked program is handed to a "recipe" that draws it with
fixed-function state. Only the programs a recipe knows are drawn (the
first: WebKit's TextureMapper compositing); programs should reach GLES
through eglGetProcAddress or dlopen, not by linking -lGLESv2.
